**Recommended role setup for safe SharePoint access**

The two organization-level roles serve distinct purposes — and both shape SharePoint exposure:

* **Org owner — complete control.** The only role that governs the SharePoint integration: which sites Normain can access at all, and which sites are connected to which teams. Whoever holds Org owner defines Normain's entire SharePoint data surface.

* **Org manager — user and team administration.** Manages who belongs to which team, team billing/usage statistics, and general org administration. An Org manager cannot touch the SharePoint integration — but since team membership is what grants access to a connected site, the Org manager indirectly controls who sees which SharePoint files.

1. **Keep Org owner tightly held** — a small number of trusted KPMG administrators. This role alone wires SharePoint sites to teams, so it defines the whole exposure.
2. **Assign Org manager to authorized access approvers** — they cannot change SharePoint connections, but they control team membership, the second access lever. Limit it to people entitled to make team-access decisions.
3. **Team owner and Team member carry no SharePoint management permissions** — granting these roles does not widen exposure.

Net: SharePoint exposure is set by two levers — site-to-team connections (**Org owner**) and team membership (**Org manager**). Keep both org roles with trusted KPMG administrators; Team owner and Team member can be distributed freely. This fits the one-site-per-engagement model we discussed.

Happy to walk through any of this or adjust the model to your governance requirements.

